{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2001-05-23T00:00:00+00:00", "id": "62858", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/62858?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/62858?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/62858?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/62858?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/62858?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/62858?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A62858"}, "updated": "2023-03-06T13:52:47.234871+00:00", "metadata": {"publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "25", "page_end": "969", "year": 1970, "journal_record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214495"}, "page_start": "966", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.Lett."}], "authors": [{"full_name": "Frishman, Y."}], "texkeys": ["Frishman:1970fx"], "abstracts": [{"value": "Consequences of the assumption that current commutators have power-type singularities near the light cone are derived. An extension of Wilson's short-distance expansion of commutators is suggested for almost lightlike distances. Consequences for power-type singularities are derived for processes involving currents. Especially, generalized scaling laws are obtained for inelastic electron-nucleon scattering. The connection with Regge behavior is discussed. An application to electron-positron annihilation into hadrons is also made."}], "control_number": 62858, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.25.966"}], "titles": [{"title": "Scale invariance and current commutators near the light cone"}], "author_count": 1, "document_type": ["article"]}}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.Lett.%2C25%2C966&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,publication_info,arxiv_eprints.value,dois.value,texkeys,abstracts.value